{#
  BeMart generic HTML error page.

  Rendered by MyVendor\BeMart\Provide\Error\HtmlThrowableHandler in the
  html context when a request maps to a known HTTP status (400 / 401 /
  403 / 404 / 409 / 422 / ...). Unexpected 500s go through the framework
  error handler (dev: stack trace, prod: generic page) instead.

  Deliberately self-contained — no `extends`, no external data — so the
  page renders even when an error happens before layout context (shop
  name, navigation, session) is available. Variables: code (int),
  statusText (string), message (string). Autoescaped by the Twig env.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="ja">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ code }} {{ statusText }} - BeMart</title>
  <style>
    body { margin: 0; background: #f7f7f9; color: #1f2937;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, "Hiragino Kaku Gothic ProN", "Noto Sans JP", sans-serif; }
    .error { max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem; text-align: center; }
    .error__code { margin: 0; font-size: 4rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; color: #d1d5db; }
    .error__status { margin: .5rem 0 1rem; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .error__message { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #4b5563; }
    .error__home { display: inline-block; padding: .6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: .375rem;
      background: #2563eb; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; }
    .error__home:hover { background: #1d4ed8; }
  </style>
</head>
<body id="error-page">
  <main class="error">
    <p class="error__code">{{ code }}</p>
    <h1 class="error__status">{{ statusText }}</h1>
    <p class="error__message">{{ message }}</p>
    <a class="error__home" href="/">トップへ戻る</a>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
